[
    "Epidermolysis Bullosa (EB) is primarily a genetic condition caused by a faulty or mutated gene.",
    "These genes are responsible for producing essential proteins that bind the skin layers together.",
    "When these proteins are missing or do not function correctly, the skin becomes fragile and blisters easily.",
    "EB can be inherited from parents or occur due to a spontaneous gene mutation.",
    "In rare cases, a severe form called Epidermolysis Bullosa Acquisita (EBA) can be acquired as an autoimmune disease.",
    "In EBA, the body's immune system mistakenly attacks its own healthy skin tissue.",
    "More detailed information on the causes of EB is available on the DEBRA UK website at https://www.debra.org.uk/get-support/eb-support-and-resources/epidermolysis-bullosa-eb/."
] 

